  "body": "## What changed\n\nA post now writes only for what its setup's machine can run (#1232):\n\n- **Kind door** (`crates/app/src/posting_serves.rs`, wired into `post_setup`/`post_script`, `post_mounts`/`post_mounts_script`, `post_per_op`/`post_per_op_script` - so the GUI, script verb and MCP `post` get it too): a mount whose post does not serve its machine's kind is refused by name (setup, ops, post, machine, kind) before anything is written. Shipped posts are judged by the picker's law (`post_serves`); a user's script by its `capabilities` mask (`work_voice`).\n- **Section door** (maintainer's decision, 2026-11-12, \"Refuse it\"): a section that turns the work - a turning op or an on-centre drill, as `lathe_voice::voice_of` reads it - posts only through a turning post (`work_voice` = `WorkSpindle`). Through a milling post it is refused by name, on a mill-turn as on a lathe. Milling and C-axis sections on a mill-turn still post through a milling post. The shipped Mill-turn machine's default post is unchanged.\n- ~27 lathe tests in 14 suites were themselves posting through the Fanuc mill post (this bug); they now select Fanuc Lathe. `lathe_cross_drill`: the generate-only tests stay on the plain lathe; only the posting test uses a mill-turn. `lathe_work_spindle`: the on-centre drill on a mill-turn through the Fanuc mill post is now refused. `lathe_stroke`: the built-in Mill-turn turning job selects Fanuc Lathe.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `post_serves_kind`: `an_own_milling_post_on_a_lathe_setup_is_refused_by_name`, `a_lathe_program_through_a_milling_post_is_refused_on_every_single_file_path`, `a_mill_setup_on_a_lathe_post_is_refused_and_the_lathe_on_its_lathe_post_still_posts`, `an_edm_mount_refuses_a_cutting_program_by_name`, `a_turning_section_on_a_mill_turn_through_a_milling_post_is_refused_by_name` (Haas own post and Fanuc document post, on post_mounts, post_per_op and post_setup; nothing written; a turning post serves it).\n- `lathe_workholding_mill_post`: `a_mill_turn_facing_op_through_a_milling_post_is_refused_and_held_to_the_chuck` (was \"posts at the chuck limit\"; now refused by name at the limit too - stricter). `a_mill_turn_milling_section_through_a_milling_post_is_not_judged` and the kind x dialect x section walk still pass (milling section on a mill-turn through Fanuc/Haas posts).\n- No golden, recorded post stream or snapshot touched: a lathe on a lathe post, a mill, and C-axis sections post byte-identical.\n\n## How tested\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head, plus `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` on head d1fec88a: whole app crate (shared `tests/common/bore.rs` maps quick to every suite) 2313 passed, 0 failed, 20 ignored (heavy lane); clippy clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe `crates/ui` suites (UI code untouched), the release-tier heavy lanes, MCP/script end to end (they call the gated entry points). Not addressed here (review notes, non-blocking): the undeclared-script hint to settle with #1213, a label for a script handed by path, a builtin-mask agreement unit test, the `lathe_workholding_kinds` test name.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nChangelog: A post now refuses by name a setup whose machine kind it does not serve, and a turning section (turning op or on-centre drill) through a milling post on a lathe or mill-turn; existing documents with a lathe or mill-turn turning op on the default Fanuc post now refuse until a turning post is picked (#1232).\n\nFixes #1232\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
